{
  "_note": "CANONICAL CLUB VISUAL IDENTITY. This file holds VISUAL metadata only — colours used to art-direct fixture graphics. Factual football metadata about opponents (ground, founded, nickname) stays in data/opponents.json, which is human-verified and must never be polluted with inferred design data. Two files, two kinds of truth.\n\nHOW A PALETTE BECOMES REAL: colours start null. js/brand-palette.js can SUGGEST a palette by sampling the club crest, and a suggestion is only ever a starting point — it lands as verified:false. A human opens Studio > Brand Library, looks at it beside the crest, edits if needed and confirms. Confirming sets verified:true. Locking sets locked:true, after which nothing automatic may overwrite it, ever.\n\nWHY THE CARE: these colours are published under the Rayners Lane badge on graphics naming another club. Getting a club’s colours wrong is the visual equivalent of misspelling their name. An unverified palette is therefore never used on its own — the engine falls back to a neutral Rayners Lane treatment until a human has said yes.",
  "_fallback": {
